# `model-bench`

**Local-first CLI analytics engine for Agentic AI models.**

[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10%2B-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)](LICENSE)

---

## What is model-bench?

Builders of Agentic AI systems face rapid model churn, complex pricing tiers, and varying capability support across **460+ models** and **50+ providers**. `model-bench` solves this by giving you a single CLI tool that:

- **Syncs** live model data from the [OpenRouter API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models) into a local SQLite database
- **Tracks** historical price changes across sync runs
- **Filters** models by provider, modality, context window, pricing, tool support, and more
- **Simulates** real workload costs with prompt-caching support
- **Ranks** models by capability-per-dollar efficiency (Pareto value ranking)
- **Exports** results to Markdown or CSV for reports and documentation

Everything runs **offline** after the initial sync — no API keys, no accounts, no cloud dependencies.

---

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10 or higher
- Linux / macOS / WSL terminal

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/manthan984/model-bench-cli.git
cd model-bench-cli

# Create a virtual environment and install
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
```

### First Run

```bash
# 1. Fetch the latest model catalog from OpenRouter
model-bench sync

# 2. View market overview
model-bench stats

# 3. Browse models
model-bench list --limit 10

# 4. Simulate costs for an agentic workflow
model-bench simulate --input-tokens 10000 --output-tokens 1500 --calls-per-day 500

# 5. Find the best value models
model-bench rank --metric agentic --limit 10
```

---

## Commands at a Glance

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `model-bench sync` | Fetch & sync the OpenRouter model catalog to local SQLite |
| `model-bench stats` | Display market KPI dashboard with distributions |
| `model-bench list` | List models with powerful multi-criteria filters |
| `model-bench simulate` | Simulate daily/monthly costs for a workload profile |
| `model-bench rank` | Rank models by capability-to-cost efficiency |

All read commands (`stats`, `list`, `simulate`, `rank`) work **fully offline** after an initial `sync`.

> 📖 For detailed usage of every command and flag, see the **[User Guide](docs/USER_GUIDE.md)**.

